		color: #ece9e0;
	}
	.wb-slider {
		accent-color: #931128;
		height: 6px;
	}
	/* THE INSTRUMENT LABEL: a caption on the machine, always visible, never a
	   warning. Quiet on purpose - the h1 already carries the loud voice, and a
	   second shouted label beside it is the "everything is emphasised" problem
	   this page is being fixed for. */
	.wb-instrument {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		max-width: 52ch;
		padding-left: 0.75rem;
		border-left: 2px solid var(--weathered-teal);
		font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
		font-size: var(--type-meta);
		font-weight: 500;
		line-height: 1.6;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--zinc-dust);
	}
	/* The disclosure that holds the full boundary text. A native <details>, so
	   it opens without JavaScript and its text is in the document either way -
	   the reader chooses how much of the contract to read, and search engines
	   still index all of it. */
	.wb-details {
		border-top: 1px solid var(--outline-oxblood);
		padding-top: var(--space-reading);
	}
	.wb-details-summary {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		gap: 0.6rem;
		cursor: pointer;
		list-style: none;
		font-family: "JetBrains Mono", monospace;
		font-size: var(--type-meta);
		font-weight: 700;
		letter-spacing: 0.14em;
		text-transform: uppercase;
		color: var(--stamped-canary);
	}
	.wb-details-summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}
	.wb-details-summary::before {
		content: "+";
		color: var(--weathered-teal);
	}
	.wb-details[open] .wb-details-summary::before {
		content: "\2212";
	}
	.wb-details-summary:hover {
		color: var(--bone-white);
	}
	/* A reference line: the sentence that tells a reader where the real
	   behaviour lives, in the voice of a citation rather than of a claim. */
	.wb-ref {
		max-width: 62ch;
		font-family: "DM Sans", sans-serif;
		font-size: var(--type-caption);
